+/// Whether Renderer::render() may leave out the screen rows whose pixels provably did not change since
+/// the previous frame.
+///
+/// Opt-in: a caller whose RenderTarget does not keep the previous frame's pixels -- one that clears its
+/// surface every frame, as a GL swap chain does -- must keep FullFrame, or the rows left out render blank.
+enum class RenderDirtyMode : uint8_t
+{
+    /// Emit draw commands for every visible cell and line, every frame.
+    FullFrame,
+    /// Leave out the page rows whose render cells and lines are identical to the previous render() call's
+    /// and that the cursor neither left nor entered. The RenderTarget must retain the pixels of the rows
+    /// left out. @see Renderer::lastDirtyRows
+    SkipUnchangedRows,
+};
